# Agent routing

Custom agents live in `.cursor/agents/`. Use them instead of one giant chat doing research, implementation, and release notes at once.

| Agent | Job |
|-------|-----|
| `sys-arch` | Research, threat model, `PLAN.md`. No `passkey/` or `tests/` edits. |
| `sys-engineer` | Implement and test. `uv` only. Mock auth. Execute `PLAN.md`. |
| `sys-release` | **Every branch/PR:** classify patch/minor/major, update `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`, bump version. |
| `sys-review` | Read-only pre-PR review. Block if changelog or version missing. |

## Required PR loop

1. `sys-arch` (if design is open) → 2. `sys-engineer` → 3. `sys-release` → 4. `sys-review` → 5. then `gh pr create`.

A project hook denies `gh pr create` and `git push` when `CHANGELOG.md` is unchanged vs `main`.

Until 1.0: patch = fix/docs/tests/CI; minor = feature or 0.x breaking change; major = 1.0.0 only. First tag is 0.4.0; before that bump 0.3.x.

Do not invent CI green, PyPI, or 1.0. `PLAN.md` is the roadmap.
